it's been about eight months since i got  my 2019 mac pro which retails at a  massive  fifteen thousand dollars and it's been  doing a killer job editing videos in  pure silence  thanks to the excellent cooling system  but now that i've spent a few weeks with  apple's new 2025k imac it performs  so well that i started wondering if i  even need it anymore  in fact we are building a new home and i  need as much cash as possible  so if this 3500 imac can get close to  the performance of my mac pro for the  tasks that i do  daily then i'm definitely going to sell  it in pocket about 10 grand  which will be perfect for a nice home  theater setup we'll be looking at a wide  variety of uses such as logic pro xcode  photo editing with photoshop and  lightroom video editing  gaming and much more i'll tell you up  front that these tests were really  eye-opening both in favor of the mac pro  and against it  and revealed a few things that i've  never known before which are going to  change the way that i'll recommend  computers forever  and that's not clickbait and i also  highly recommend  buying an ultrasoft premium max tech  shirt  or with that one of these soft  comfortable masks  if you want to support the channel and  have something that's super  comfortable first here are the full  specs of each mac  the mac pro has two extra cores but they  are an older design and run slower than  the new imacs  but will present a few surprises my mac  pro has the vega 2 graphics with 32  gigabytes of video memory compared to  the 5700 xt  with 16 gigabytes in the imac you can  also get a w5700x in the mac pro  for a fair bit less than my mega 2 and  it's a newer design  but has less raw power and half of the  memory that also runs quite a bit slower  we also have a huge difference in ram 64  gigabytes compared to 192  which i'll show you why it really  doesn't matter  now lastly my mac pro has a 2 000  afterburner card which accelerates  prores and prores raw the mac pro comes  in at about 15 grand  but i bought the ram myself bringing it  down to 13 000  which is still almost four times the  cost of the imac  which was 3540 if you buy the ram  yourself and follow our ram install  guide  which you absolutely should do i'll link  it down below along with that the 5k  imac comes with a gorgeous 5k display  that costs 1300  to add to the mac pro now there's more  to the story such as  ports cooling upgradability and more but  let's  save that for later and jump right into  performance starting off with a good old  geekbench that tests a wide variety of  tasks the imac  win in single core due to its faster  frequency but in multi-core the pro  scores closer to 30 percent  higher now putting a constant 100 cpu  load on all of the cores and cinebench  r20 which is a 3d rendering benchmark  the i9 imac shockingly beats out the mac  pro  by just over a hundred points even  though it does have two less cores  looking deeper the results actually make  sense because the mac pro runs at 3.6  gigahertz under full load  and the imac runs at 4 gigahertz which  is overall faster  and it actually uses about 150 watts to  achieve the faster speed  instead of 170 watts so it's more  efficient but with that  it also runs much hotter and louder  because of the small chassis instead of  being completely silent  as for graphics geekbench's metal  graphics test resulted in the mac pro  scoring just over 65 higher in raw  graphics performance  which is a big difference as it should  be for a graphics card that costs  almost as much as the whole imac but  hold on because  real world performance will be  interesting looking at another graphics  test this time gaming with unigine  heaven  here instead of a 65 difference the mac  pros vega 2  is only 18 faster which is a huge  difference compared to before  that's because the latest amd rda  graphics have lots of improvements  outside of raw graphics power  they're great for gaming and a few other  things as you'll notice  the mac pro is the fastest mac for  gaming it can even handle  6k gaming but the 5k imac is almost as  good  while being a fraction of the price  graphics are also great for 3d rendering  which we use  blender to test here and the difference  was even smaller at about seven percent  only being about one minute faster to  render the bmw and classroom scenes  which is very interesting let's get into  some more common uses like photo editing  using lightroom both are extremely  smooth and fast while editing  to be honest i couldn't notice any  difference  i exported 542mbps edited raw images  which maxes out the cpu so i expect the  results to be close  but what i saw was shocking the mac pro  was practically twice  as fast these results made no sense  since cinebench was  actually faster on the imac so i  searched through  everything to find a bottleneck and  surprisingly it wasn't the ram  it wasn't the ssd and after hours of  testing and researching i figured out  that the reason the mac pro is so much  faster  is its six-channel memory instead of  dual channel  the base imac pro is slower in every way  than the 5k imac and it has half the ram  yet it was actually somewhat in between  the mac pro and the imac in terms of  performance  and that uses 4 channel memory which is  also  right there in the middle onto photoshop  once again i couldn't tell  a single difference when doing my normal  work but we ran the puget bench  photoshop mix benchmark and the mac pro  smoked the 5k  imac i'm betting it's once again because  of the 6 channel memory instead of dual  channel with that said  they trade blows in certain tasks so  pause this video to see the detailed  breakdowns  before some shockers in logic pro and  xcode let's touch on something that we  do  on the daily and that's video editing  i'll be doing a detailed review  including premiere pro and davinci  resolve tests in a dedicated video on my  filmmaking channel  which i'll link down below but here i  will focus on final cut  there's certain things that this 5700 is  just so much  faster at the same thing goes for  stabilizing 4k  hevc footage where the imac was 65  faster i exported two five minute sample  projects with multiple effects  the first being common 4k h.264 and the  second being h.265  and in both cases the mac pro was faster  i then exported one of our youtube  videos which is roughly 12 minutes long  and it has a ton of graphs and effects  and the gap actually closed up here when  your gpu  has to do all of these effects and  animations  the newer 5700 is just more efficient by  the way all of these numbers are using  the latest version of final cut which  has changed some of the results from our  previous videos  getting into tougher tests like canon  raw the mac pro is still super fast for  this  taking just 5 minutes but the imac isn't  too far behind  as for editing smoothness the mac pro  can handle 4k60 raw with effects  perfectly with some more overhead for  extra effects where the imac can barely  handle 4k60 with the lut at full  resolution  but that is still enough for most c200  editors who usually work in a 24 or 30  fps timeline  moving on to red raw using the new metal  decoding the mac pro can play back this  really compressed ak  almost perfectly in an ak timeline while  the imac is just a few frames per second  behind  and both are limited by graphics not the  processors  rendering the projects i was shocked to  see that the mac pro was actually slower  at exporting my 4.5k redraw test  by just a few seconds and for the 8k  project  exporting out to 4k the imac was  actually 22  faster which is crazy now if you had the  cheaper w5700  x in your mac pro it would match up to  the imac here but would be slightly less  smooth when you're actually doing  editing compared to the vega the new  canon r5 and r6 are very popular but  their 422 footage is tough to edit  so many people are going to be  transcoding now the mac pro can convert  30 minutes of 4k  10 bit in about 30 minutes while the  imac takes 37.  surprisingly when editing in the  timeline the imac  is actually smoother with that exporting  a 5 minute project is  actually more than a minute faster using  the imac compared to the mac pro  it's another thing that i didn't expect  and that's because the cpu can run  faster at up to five gigahertz  now my mac pro does have something that  the imac will never  get and that is the two thousand dollar  afterburner card that decodes prores and  prores raw  so the cpu doesn't have to do it it's  important to note that it won't help  transcoding  since it can't encode prores but in  cases when you're going from one flavor  of prores to another like this 4k pro vs  raw project  there is a noticeable speed difference  since the cpu can focus solely on  encoding  the results are similar testing ak  prores raw to ak prores where the  afterburner equipped pro  is significantly faster but if you don't  dish out two grand for this extra card  the 10 core imac is just as fast as the  12 core mac pro  as far as playback the imac can handle  one stream of 8k  prores raw in an 8k project perfectly  smooth  exactly like the mac pro without  afterburner but neither can do  more than that with the afterburner my  mac pro can do four streams of 8k  or a single stream of 16k pro res ra  which is something that this imac will  never do so if you'll need to have an  afterburner or the ability to say by a  28 core  or have four graphics card you'll only  be able to do that  in a mac pro overall for the vast  majority of people the 5k imac with the  5700 xt  is rounding up to be an amazing bargain  for video editing  in some cases it's actually faster than  my mac pro and when it's slower  the difference isn't dramatic now what  about logic pro  x and also xcode well the results are  going to surprise you  the imac could handle 125 tracks before  shutting down on our logic benchmark  which is really respectable  and enough for most people and i  expected the mac pro to be similar  but it handled up to 227 tracks  once again probably because of memory  bandwidth the results were similar in  our custom  xcode benchmark where the mac pro was  almost twice as fast  even though the test maxed out the cpu  on both now  unlike logic though the imac pro was  slower than the imac for xcode  so i can't say it's a memory bandwidth  limitation but the mac pro  sure is fast for compiling code overall  as far as performance  this i9 5700xt imac is more than enough  for most people  even most professionals and it's much  faster than just a few years ago  massive difference with that said the  mac pro does excel if you're pushing it  to the absolute extremes and beyond  and for compiling code and exporting  photos it is much quicker  and for some of the people out there  that might be doing a ton of that  constantly on the daily it might be  worth spending three to five times as  much  depending on the configuration and your  monitor's price  along with that the mac pro is almost  dead  silent where the imac will sound like a  hair dryer and many of these rendering  tests  which does get annoying but if most of  your time is spent  editing photos and editing the video and  not constantly rendering it  then it stays mostly quiet the mac pro  also has  eight thunderbolt ports up to 12  actually depending on your graphics  instead of having two  and it has dual 10 gigabit ethernet  instead of one 10 gig ethernet  and of course it's expandable in the  future so if you're going to keep your  machine for many years that is a  definite plus  on the flip side imacs hold their value  so well  that it might actually be cheaper to  upgrade every few years to the latest  and greatest  instead of holding on to a mac pro for  say 10 years  where the value will go from 15 000 down  to just a few  i just sold my 2017 imac and it cost me  1200  to own it for three years so you could  do the math yourself there  after all of that testing the imac does  indeed get very close to the mac pro  in the daily professional tasks that i  do and it is  actually faster for editing my canon r5  footage  so with that said the mac pro is going  to be put up for sale  so if you're interested in getting a  great deal  on a mac pro let me know down in the  comment section below  if you guys want to see the full final  review of the 2020  5k imac make sure you guys click that  subscribe button up above  and check out one of these ultra premium  soft shirts down below in the merch  shelf  this has been max and i'll see you in  the next video

